nQuantum Nanoscience\nBiotechnology\nImaging Physics\nRadiation Science & Technology\nEach department has its own research programme that PhDs are regularly asked to join. To get an idea of the research programmes on offer and see some vacancies, follow the link to the various departments.\nIf you are interested in a PhD project at the faculty of Applied Sciences, we advise you to keep a close eye on the vacancy website where the latest selection of PhD vacancies can be found.\nView our vacancy website\nPhD at the TU Delft\nTU Delft Graduate School\nIf you find a suitable place and are accepted as a PhD candidate, you will encounter the TU Delft Graduate School, which supports all PhD candidates at TU Delft. The TU Delft Graduate School facilitates PhD candidates to become highly qualified, independent and leading researchers, as well as skilled professionals.\nThe Graduate School consists of a University Graduate School (UGS) and eight Faculty Graduate Schools (FGSs). Together, they support PhD candidates throughout their doctoral journey by providing a coherent training programme, supervision and administrative support. An important part of this support is high-quality supervision. In addition, PhD candidates can benefit from the knowledge and experience of PhD mentors.\nQuestions & Support\nUniversity Graduate School (UGS)\nOn the website, you can find information about, among other things, admission requirements and fees and funding.\nIf you have general questions about Graduate School processes, such as admission requirements, registration for Doctoral Education courses, or the PhD defence ceremony, please contact the University Graduate School (UGS).\nThe UGS can be reached by phone on Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday between 10:00 and 12:00.\nPhone: +31 (0)15 278 7334\nEmail: graduateschool@tudelft.nl\nFaculty Graduate School (FGS)\nFor questions about faculty-specific processes, such as your supervision team, mentors, the progress of your PhD trajectory, Doctoral Education credits, and discipline-related courses, please contact your Faculty Graduate School (FGS).\nFaculty Graduate School Applied Science (FGS-AS)\nEmail: graduateschool-TNW@tudelft.nl\nLocation: Building 22, Room F131\nIntranet: Faculty Graduate School AS - Intranet\nTNW postgraduate education\nIn addition to the PhD trajectory, that in general takes four years, the faculty also offers postgraduate education programmes that take two years and lead to an EngD title. More information on the EngD programmes can be found on TNW postgraduate education.\nShare this page:\nFacebook\nLinkedin\nTwitter\nEmail\nWhatsApp\nShare this page\nFaculty of Applied Sciences\nlinkedin\ninstagram\nfacebook\nOrganisation\nResearch departments\nFacilities\nFind employees\nVacancies\nContact and route\nBuildings AS:\nApplied Sciences (B58)\nApplied Physics (B22)\nTU Delft Reactor Institute (B50)\nIndustrial Catalysis Lab (B67)\nCampus map\nTel: +31 (0)15 27 89806\nActivate high contrast\nEducation\nBachelor programmes\nMinors and electives\nMaster programmes\nIncoming Exchange students\nResearch\nResearch areas\nStories of scientists\nPhD\nBusiness\nNeed a graduate or student?\nContract Research\nFacilities\nCourses & Postgraduate Programmes\nNews\nAgenda\nLatest News\nAbout Faculty\nDean\nProfile, facts and figures\nProfessors\nInstitutes & Research Schools\nDepartments\nPrizes\nAwards & Funding\nContact and route\nAssociations & Societies\nVacancies\nSearch", "links": [["To main content", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/faculty-of-applied-sciences/research/phd#main"], ["TU Delft homepage", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/"], ["Education", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/faculty-of-applied-sciences/education"], ["Bachelor programmes", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/faculty-of-applied-sciences/education/bachelor-programmes"], ["Minors and electives", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/faculty-of-applied-sciences/education/minors-and-electives"], ["Master programmes", "https://www.tudelft.nl/en/facult